course: dictionary
lesson: 14229
title: Narrative
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A narrative is a story, or a description of events in the order they happened. When a story has a beginning, a middle and an end, it is a narrative. «Mia told a narrative of her trip to the zoo, starting with the bus and ending with the ice cream.» The word shows that the events are told in order.
explain: Narrative can be a noun or an adjective. «Narrative writing» is writing that tells a story, with characters and a setting. «A narrative poem» tells a story in verse. The noun names the story itself, and the adjective describes the kind of writing.
explain: In the news, a narrative is the story people tell about events. «The school's narrative of the flood was different from the parents' story.» Two people can tell the same events in different ways, so a narrative can also be the version of events someone chooses to tell.
fact: A narrative is a story, or a description of events in order.
fact: «Narrative» can be a noun (a narrative) or an adjective (narrative writing).
fact: Narrative writing has characters, a setting, and a beginning, middle and end.
fact: A narrative poem is a poem that tells a story.
fact: Narrative can also mean the way a set of events is told or explained, such as «the official narrative».
exercise: Which of these is a narrative? | A list of things to buy at the shop | A map of the city centre | *A story about a dragon who finds a new friend | A sum with ten numbers
exercise: «Ben wrote a narrative about his holiday.» What does a narrative usually have? | *A beginning, a middle and an end | Pictures and no words at all | A title in capital letters only | Only a list of numbers
exercise: Tom says, «The official narrative says the bridge closed for repairs.» What does narrative mean here? | A small fish in the river | A kind of bridge made of wood | *The way events are told or explained | A quick walk to school
test: «Priya read a narrative poem about a brave knight.» What is a narrative poem? | A poem about the weather | A short list of rules | *A poem that tells a story | A poem with no words
test: Mum says, «Your narrative of the day doesn't match what your brother said.» What does narrative mean? | A snack for lunch | *The story someone tells about what happened | A type of cloud | A rule about homework
exam: «The newspaper gave one narrative of the storm, but the mayor gave another.» What does narrative mean in this sentence? | A kind of rain | A map of the town | A short poem | *The story people tell about events
